 "action_summary": "A census of the seven measurable held-out kinds that refuse at learning found exactly three failure classes: the example restructures whole statements (six kinds, intrinsic to one-showing learning), the example contradicts itself (one kind, intrinsic), and the example tangles an incidental local rename with the real lesson (np_int, the documented tangled-commit phenomenon, 11-40 percent of real commits). The third class is now fixed soundly: when the example's second file binds exactly one plainly assigned non-builtin name the first does not and vice versa, and neither name is ever an import, def, class, parameter, or global in its file, the rename is undone before learning and the lesson underneath becomes visible. Import renames, def renames, parameter renames, double renames, and rename-only examples are never set aside.",
